From: Rakina Zata Amni <rakina@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 01:33:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/22] [M156] Use one directory database per first-party
 default bucket

Original change's description:
> Use one directory database per first-party default bucket
>
> The directory of a first-party default bucket only depends on its
> StorageKey, but ObfuscatedFileUtil's DatabaseKey also included the
> bucket ID. When the default bucket is deleted and recreated (e.g. by
> Clear-Site-Data), a URL with the old ID (from a stale FileSystemAccess
> handle, or a legacy FileSystem operation that re-cached the old default
> bucket mid-deletion) and a URL with the new ID got different keys for
> the same directory, so two SandboxDirectoryDatabases were opened on it.
> In off-the-record profiles the in-memory LevelDB Env doesn't enforce
> locks, so both instances ran and overwrote each other's files.
>
> Make DatabaseKey ignore the bucket ID for first-party default buckets,
> matching how their directory is chosen, so there's only ever one
> database per directory. Third-party and non-default buckets already
> have a separate directory per bucket ID and are unaffected.
>
> Fixed: 574852697, 581367285
